{
  "_README": {
    "purpose": "Declarative bar-shape library for the BBS shape drawer.",
    "how_to_add_a_shape": [
      "Add an entry to the 'shapes' array below.",
      "Coordinates are NORMALISED 0..1 across the drawing canvas:",
      "  x = 0 is left edge, x = 1 is right edge.",
      "  y = 0 is TOP edge, y = 1 is BOTTOM edge.",
      "A built-in padding is applied so 0..1 maps to the usable area.",
      "",
      "Each shape has:",
      "  id        - unique key (used by quick buttons + saved sketches)",
      "  label     - text shown on the quick-shape button",
      "  bs8666    - the BS 8666 shape code (string, optional, shown as caption)",
      "  formula   - cutting-length formula text (optional caption)",
      "  group     - 'quick' to show as a quick button, or any category name",
      "  segments  - array of polyline segments to render. Each segment:",
      "      pts    : [[x,y], [x,y], ...] normalised points",
      "      style  : 'bend' (arc bends) | 'straight' (sharp) | 'curve' (spline)",
      "      closed : true to close the loop back to the first point (optional)",
      "  dims      - array of dimension lines: {from:[x,y], to:[x,y], label, off:[dx,dy]}",
      "",
      "ISOMETRIC shapes: set iso:true and give points as [x,y,z] world units.",
      "Auto-projected at 30deg and auto-centred. 'fit' sets world scale.",
      "Iso dims must also set iso:true and use [x,y,z] from/to.",
      "",
      "PARAMETRIC shapes: set generator:'circle' or 'spiral' (turns applies to spiral).",
      "",
      "NOTE: bbs/shape-library.js holds an embedded copy so the app works from",
      "disk (file://). When served over http THIS file overrides it.",
      "",
      "TIP: You can DRAW a shape in the drawer, then click 'Export to shapes.json'",
      "to generate a ready-to-paste entry (auto-normalised to 0..1). Paste it into",
      "the 'shapes' array below and run: node bbs/build-shapes.js"
    ],
    "schema_version": 2
  },
